author ai
group features/gui
note The 'delete' button on a step header removes that step from the tour being read; the steps under it move up to its parent. The reader reaches for it to undo a wrongly added step from the document, without switching to the CLI (deleting is in the document). The status bar names what was removed, the selection is cleared, and the map is marked unsaved until ctrl+s or the save button writes it. Steps shown inline under a link have no delete button. There is no undo, so a delete button that arrives under a resting pointer because the document re-laid out does not fire until the pointer moves.

